--- queue src's current texture into dst as a sprite CENTERED at (x, y), under dst's transform stack: layer_draw_texture for a layer, so one layer can be drawn into another rotated, scaled or flipped (layer_draw_into only fills an axis-aligned rect, immediately). The command carries the texture id at queue time, so render src before dst. FBO textures are stored bottom-up: push a y-scale of -1 to draw one upright. The replay recorder writes it as a layer reference (apr_texref_for), so recordings play it back.
---@param dst lightuserdata|table
---@param src lightuserdata|table
---@param x number
---@param y number
---@param color? integer
function layer_draw_layer(dst, src, x, y, color) end

--- draw src layer's current color texture into a RECT of dst's FBO (top-left game coords in dst space), scaled to w x h. The viewport variant of layer_draw_from: same screen shader and orientation (proven FBO->FBO path), but the fullscreen quad rasterizes only inside the rect. Rects partially outside dst clip naturally. This is the embedded-game composite: a fixed-size game layer placed into the site's document layer at the element's on-screen rect.
---@param dst lightuserdata|table
---@param src lightuserdata|table
---@param x number
---@param y number
---@param w number
---@param h number
function layer_draw_into(dst, src, x, y, w, h) end

